# Tools the CI gate checks for on a venue before it runs this suite.
#
# The list is DERIVED from the suite by ci-gate.sh (it reads the spawn calls in
# test/ and reports the binaries it believes are needed). This file only
# CORRECTS that derivation: a bare name adds a tool the scan cannot see, a
# leading `-` drops a false positive.
#
# DELETE is SQL, not a binary. test/unit/db.reorg-real-ddl.test.js passes
# `DELETE FROM blocks; DELETE FROM index_transactions;` to sqlite.exec(), and
# the scan reads the leading word of that string as a command name. The gate
# then blocks every push with a VENUE TOOLING GAP for a tool no venue can ever
# have, so this is a false positive that never self-heals.
-DELETE
